{{!-- Packagist: Private Packagist call to action at the end of every post (AMK-5).
Posts tagged "Private Packagist" or "changelog" get the trial pitch, all other posts the
softer "Using Composer at work?" variant. Add the internal tag #no-cta to a post to hide it,
for example on posts that already end with their own sign-up section.
The links carry UTM parameters so Plausible on packagist.com shows which variant and which
post sent each visitor. --}}
{{^has tag="#no-cta"}}
<aside class="pp-cta gh-canvas">
    <div class="pp-cta-box">
    {{#has tag="Private Packagist, changelog"}}
        <h2 class="pp-cta-title">Try Private Packagist free for 14 days</h2>
        <p>Private Packagist is the Composer repository for your team: private packages, mirrors of Packagist.org and third-party repositories, security monitoring, and organization-wide policies. No credit card needed for the trial.</p>
        <a class="pp-cta-button" href="https://packagist.com/?utm_source=blog.packagist.com&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=cta-product&amp;utm_content={{slug}}">Start your free trial</a>
    {{else}}
        <h2 class="pp-cta-title">Using Composer at work?</h2>
        <p>Composer and Packagist.org are maintained by the team behind Private Packagist, and Private Packagist subscriptions fund that work. Private Packagist gives your team private packages, mirrors of Packagist.org and third-party repositories, and security monitoring. Free for 14 days.</p>
        <a class="pp-cta-button" href="https://packagist.com/?utm_source=blog.packagist.com&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=cta-composer&amp;utm_content={{slug}}">Learn about Private Packagist</a>
    {{/has}}
    </div>
</aside>
{{/has}}
